SUMMARY:National Theatre Live: The Fifth Step
DESCRIPTION:National Theatre Live – On Screen\nThe Fifth Step\nBy David Ireland\nDirected by Finn den Hertog\nAfter years in the 12-step progrm of Alcoholics Anonymous\, James becomes a sponsor to newcomer Luka. The pair bond over black coffee\, trade stories and build a fragile friendship out of their shared experiences. But as Luka approaches step five – the moment of confession – dangerous truths emerge\, threatening the trust on which both of their recoveries depend.\nFinn den Hertog directs the provocative and entertaining production filmed live from Soho Theatre on London’s West End.\nAge Rating:R (due to due to strong language\, sexual themes\, and intense discussions regarding addiction)\nRunning Time: 90 minutes (no intermission)\nGeneral admission (unreserved seating).\nThe historic Shepherdstown Opera House is a cozy 99-seat vaudeville-era theater — we encourage patrons to purchase tickets in advance. Online sales end 1 hour before showtime. Doors open 30 minutes before showtime and our shows start promptly. Popcorn\, candy\, soft drinks\, beer & wine available for purchase (no outside food or drinks please). Lobby\, theater & restroom are wheelchair accessible.\n
LOCATION:Shepherdstown Opera House, 131 West German Street, Shepherdstown
URL:https://operahouselive.com/apr-26-national-theatre-live-the-fifth-step/
CATEGORIES:Film & Performing Arts
ORGANIZATION:Shepherdstown Opera House
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SOURCE:operahouselive.com
SEQUENCE:0
END:VEVENT
