SUMMARY:All The President’s Men
DESCRIPTION:All The President’s Men (1976) — 50th Anniversary Screening\n2026 Academy Award Winner for Best Documentary Feature.\nCast: Robert Redford\, Dustin Hoffman\, Jason Robards\, Jack Warden\, Martin Balsam\nMark the 50th anniversary of the release of All the President’s Men\, the acclaimed journalistic drama based on the reporting of Washington Post journalists Bob Woodward and Carl Bernstein\, whose investigation helped uncover the Watergate scandal and led to President Nixon’s resignation.\nA post-film discussion will allow the audience to explore Watergate-related memories\, the film’s legacy\, and the continuing importance of investigative journalism.\nOptional: Guests are welcome to embrace the spirit of 1970s Washington DC — think newsroom reporters and Capitol Hill professionals\, with blazers\, wide ties\, trench coats\, shirt dresses\, note pads\, oversized glasses\, and printed newspapers under their arm.\nYear Released: 1976\nRating: PG\nRuntime: 138 minutes\nLanguage: English\nTickets: Pay-What-You-Can ($10 suggested). Presented in partnership with Shepherd University’s Lifelong Learning Program – A volunteer member-driven program dedicated to offering stimulating academic courses and activities to the community.\nThe historic Shepherdstown Opera House is a cozy 99-seat vaudeville-era theater — we encourage patrons to purchase tickets in advance. Online sales end 1 hour before showtime. Doors open 30 minutes before showtime and our shows start promptly. Popcorn\, candy\, soft drinks\, beer & wine available for purchase (no outside food or drinks please). Lobby\, theater & restroom are wheelchair accessible.\n
LOCATION:Shepherdstown Opera House, 131 West German Street, Shepherdstown
URL:https://operahouselive.com/may-3-all-the-presidents-men/
CATEGORIES:Film & Performing Arts
ORGANIZATION:Shepherdstown Opera House
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SOURCE:operahouselive.com
