SUMMARY:Dara James and the Soul Disciples
DESCRIPTION:Dara James and the Soul Disciples is an award-winning Central Virginia-based organ trio known for their powerhouse blend of blues\, funk\, R&B\, and soul. \nThe band features Dara James (Guitar\, Vocals)\, Eric Franzen (Hammond Organ)\, and Jeff Louderback (Drums). Lead singer Dara James began his professional career at age 11 as a harmonica player and previously played with the Jon Spear Band.\nTheir performances feature award-winning original songwriting alongside “refreshing” covers of classic rock and soul artists like Stevie Wonder\, Curtis Mayfield\, and Hall & Oates.\nThe band has released several critically acclaimed albums that have earned them a stack of Washington Area Music Awards (WAMMIES). Their discography reflects their journey from blues purists to masters of a “blues-infused” hybrid sound:\nThe group reached the semi-finals of the International Blues Challenge in Memphis in early 2026.\nArtist website: DaraJonesMusic.com\nThe historic Shepherdstown Opera House is a cozy 99-seat vaudeville-era theater — we encourage patrons to purchase tickets in advance. Online sales end 1 hour before showtime. Doors open 30 minutes before showtime and our shows start promptly. Popcorn\, candy\, soft drinks\, beer & wine available for purchase (no outside food or drinks please). Lobby\, theater & restroom are wheelchair accessible.\n
LOCATION:Shepherdstown Opera House, 131 West German Street, Shepherdstown
URL:https://operahouselive.com/may-22-dara-james-and-the-soul-disciples/
CATEGORIES:Film & Performing Arts
ORGANIZATION:Shepherdstown Opera House
STATUS:CONFIRMED
