SUMMARY:Jamie Turner & Those Revelators
DESCRIPTION:Jamie Alan Turner is a seasoned musician whose music traverses the rich tapestry of Folk\, Americana\, and Blues music. With over two decades of musical experience\, Jamie’s compositions and evocative performances transport audiences on a journey through the heartland of American roots music. His skillful guitar work harkens back to the greats of these genres while carving a unique path of his own.\nInfluenced by a diverse array of musical legends\, Jamie’s music reflects the essence of artists who have shaped the sound of a generation. From the gritty authenticity of Delta Blues to the storytelling traditions of American Folk\, his music pays homage to these timeless influences while adding a modern twist.\nJamie Turner and Those Revelators is Jamie on guitar\, Rob Adaire on bass and Nick Kline tapping the drums. They are all very experienced musicians with Jamie having over 30 years of guitar under his belt\, Rob and they play contemporary blues rock – their own tunes and those by bands that have recently graced the blues charts.\nArtist website: JamieTurnerMusic.com\nThe historic Shepherdstown Opera House is a cozy 99-seat vaudeville-era theater — we encourage patrons to purchase tickets in advance. Online sales end 1 hour before showtime. Doors open 30 minutes before showtime and our shows start promptly. Popcorn\, candy\, soft drinks\, beer & wine available for purchase (no outside food or drinks please). Lobby\, theater & restroom are wheelchair accessible.\n
LOCATION:Shepherdstown Opera House, 131 West German Street, Shepherdstown
URL:https://operahouselive.com/may-29-jamie-turner-those-revelators/
